Subject: [PATCH] Bypass ICD verification

The current R8 build inlined argument construction into attestKey and
AttestParameterSpec no longer has the old constructor. Keep every current
field, builder, consumer and descriptor; change only the ICD capability
input at its actual use, as the original patch intended. Retain challenge,
alias, certificate, KeyMint error handling, permissions and SAK UID rules.
Do not fabricate keys or return successful attestation without the service.

diff --git a/smali_classes2/com/samsung/android/security/keystore/AttestationUtils.smali b/smali_classes2/com/samsung/android/security/keystore/AttestationUtils.smali
--- a/smali_classes2/com/samsung/android/security/keystore/AttestationUtils.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/com/samsung/android/security/keystore/AttestationUtils.smali
@@ -355,21 +355,21 @@
     move-result-object v0
 
     const v3, -0x6ffff7ca
 
     invoke-static {v3, v0}, Lcom/samsung/android/security/keystore/AttestationUtils;->makeBytes(I[B)Landroid/hardware/security/keymint/KeyParameter;
 
     move-result-object v0
 
     invoke-virtual {v1, v0}, Ljava/util/ArrayList;->add(Ljava/lang/Object;)Z
 
-    iget-boolean v0, p1, Lcom/samsung/android/security/keystore/AttestParameterSpec;->mVerifiableIntegrity:Z
+    const/4 v0, 0x1
 
     const-string v3, "AttestationUtils"
 
     if-eqz v0, :cond_9
 
     const v0, 0x700008fe
 
     invoke-static {v0}, Lcom/samsung/android/security/keystore/AttestationUtils;->makeBool(I)Landroid/hardware/security/keymint/KeyParameter;
 
     move-result-object v0

